Item 11 is done and the loop stands at 11 of 13.

**What was proved.** All three targets of the item are in Lean, in one new file `lean/MOSPFormalization/ForestCover.lean`, imported by the root module, with no `sorry`, no `axiom`, and every theorem on the three standard axioms only.

- **F1, the blow-up lemma.** The incidence graph of an instance as a graph on customers plus patterns, and a path decomposition of the MOSP graph built from any decomposition of it. The MOSP form holds for every instance with no hypothesis: the MOSP value is at most the largest pattern times one more than the incidence graph's pathwidth. The forest form follows through the tree size bound, with the §6 integer identity for the log form proved as the least such index.
- **The coupling inclusion** of item 10. An empty pair of a larger cover's graph is an empty pair of the smaller cover's graph, and pathwidth is monotone in the cover. Subinstance monotonicity of the MOSP value came free, which formalises the proposition behind the relaxation code.
- **The layer lemma** of item 07, generalised to any level function in which adjacent vertices differ by at most one. BFS distance from a root is one such function, so the BFS form of the report is a corollary. The vertex separation of the specific layer-by-layer order is not what is proved, and the report says so.

**Checks.** The Lean definitions are pinned to the record through a new stage of `learning/sandwich.py`: zero violations on all 4,419 rows of item 03's record, slack at least one everywhere, and the log form identity on every size to 3,000. Seven new tests brute-force each statement on tiny instances with no solver and nothing persisted. The paper's axiom check gained 13 lines and prints 260 lines with no `sorryAx`. Nothing was solved and `solutions/` was not touched.

